# XCU type
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# type is intrinsic (XCU 1.7) and shaded XSI on its SYNOPSIS. Its output
# format is unspecified, so tests judge exit status and that something is
# written for each operand.

assertion  XCU.type.001
anchor     utilities/type.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     utilities/type.html#STDOUT
anchor     utilities/type.html#EXIT STATUS
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1992
says       type for a utility found through PATH exits zero and writes
           something to standard output.
test       t/001-utility.sh

assertion  XCU.type.002
anchor     utilities/type.html#EXIT STATUS
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1992
says       type for a name that no command search finds exits greater than
           zero.
test       t/002-not-found.sh

assertion  XCU.type.003
anchor     utilities/type.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     utilities/type.html#STDOUT
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1992
says       type for a shell function and for an alias exits zero and
           writes something to standard output for each.
test       t/003-function-alias.sh

assertion  XCU.type.004
anchor     utilities/type.html#OPERANDS
anchor     utilities/type.html#STDOUT
anchor     utilities/type.html#EXIT STATUS
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1992
says       With several operands, type writes information for each name it
           knows (the output grows with every operand found) and exits
           greater than zero when any operand is not found.
test       t/004-several.sh
